WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:08.559
When the History Channel decided to base a
series around people cutting down trees, none

00:00:08.559 --> 00:00:12.820
of us could have imagined the colorful characters
they'd introduce to the world.

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:17.000
The excitement doesn't end when the Ax Men
cameras stop rolling, either.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:21.810
Here are just a few of the things the show's
producers didn't catch on film.

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:24.429
JImmy Smith’s Illegal Salvage

00:00:24.429 --> 00:00:31.189
Back in 2009, S&amp;S Aqua Logging got into some
hot water with the Department of Natural Resources

00:00:31.189 --> 00:00:34.600
for illegally salvaging wood from a river.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:39.260
As sunken logs become an integral part of
a river bed, removing them can cause a lot

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:41.080
of damage the ecosystem.

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:47.210
DNR officers became suspicious of S&amp;S after
seeing them do some shady stuff on an episode

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:48.250
of Ax Men.

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:54.000
So, for future reference, committing a crime
on TV is a really bad idea.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:59.559
To prevent further harm, DNR officials seized
over two dozen logs from S&amp;S.

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:05.510
Unfortunately for company owner Jimmy Smith,
this wasn't the end of his troubles...

00:01:05.510 --> 00:01:06.510
Disability Fraud

00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:13.160
In addition to stealing wood, Jimmy Smith
allegedly bilked more than $50,000 in fraudulent

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:14.950
disability benefits.

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:19.490
During the time Smith salvaged the timber
in question, he was also collecting medical

00:01:19.490 --> 00:01:24.760
benefits for two claims he filed with the
Department of Labor and Industries, one from

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:28.350
1993 and another from 1996.

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:32.740
According to a surgeon, Smith had complained
of "Impairments" in his "shoulders, neck,

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:35.790
back, or any other portions of the extremities."

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:40.200
In other words, things that would prevent
him from cutting and moving large pieces of

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:44.410
wood and equipment, as he was seen doing on
television.

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:47.600
His trouble with the law didn't last much
longer, though.

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:54.120
After pleading guilty to the fraud allegations
in 2011, Smith passed away in 2012.

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:55.840
Katelyn Sims’ illness

00:01:55.840 --> 00:02:00.980
While some loggers have been accused of cashing
in on injuries they don't have, Katelyn Sims

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:03.090
is the exact opposite.

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:08.700
The young logger has battled cystic fibrosis,
a terminal illness, since she was four.

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:13.210
She doesn't let that stop her from felling
and moving trees, however, making some of

00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:16.660
her male counterparts look like wimps in the
process.

00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:22.110
To fight the disease's effects, Sims undergoes
regular treatments, allowing her to keep active

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:25.780
and continue working, increasing her odds
of survival.

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:28.330
Sims also uses her fame to help spread CF
awareness.

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:29.330
"My name is Katelyn Sims.

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:35.760
I'm a Cystic Fibrosis advocate, and I'm a
student at Sante Fe College."

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:38.140
This is one tough lady.

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:40.470
Death of a logger

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:45.620
Logging is dangerous work, and some of Ax
Men's stars have, sadly, lost their lives

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:46.840
on the job.

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:52.760
Helicopter logger Bart Colantuono died in
2013 while attempting to airlift some lumber

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:54.030
in Oregon.

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:59.280
According to witnesses, a rotor came off his
chopper, which then flipped upside down.

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:02.730
The incident prompted a lengthy investigation.

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:04.819
Mike Pihl’s arrest

00:03:04.819 --> 00:03:07.850
Logging seems to attract unusual personalities.

00:03:07.850 --> 00:03:13.150
Such is the case with Mike Pihl, owner of
the aptly-named Mike Pihl Logging.

00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:19.740
In 2009, Pihl got into an alcohol-induced
fender bender and flipped his Jeep, injuring

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:21.470
three of his kids.

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:27.160
Since the accident occurred on private property,
the police filed no DUI charges, but they

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:30.130
did charge Pihl with felony assault.

00:03:30.130 --> 00:03:34.100
Fortunately, Pihl hasn’t been in any trouble
since.

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:36.209
Roger Gunter’s poaching

00:03:36.209 --> 00:03:41.709
Master diver Roger Gunter has been caught
six times for hunting without a license.

00:03:41.709 --> 00:03:47.630
Before he gained fame on Ax Men, Gunter was
already a well-known Florida monkey fisher.

00:03:47.630 --> 00:03:53.220
For the uninitiated, "monkey fishing" refers
to fishing using electricity...

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:55.200
not fishing for actual monkeys.

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:59.560
He was caught six times over a 30-to-40 year
span.

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:05.130
But since then, Gunter has apparently mended
his ways, even befriending the local authorities

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:07.230
with whom he once butted heads.

00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:12.900
"It's a really unlikely friendship, considering
Bob spent his career not trying to catch fish,

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:14.140
but trying to catch Roger."

00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:17.470
"Well I don't chase him anymore, and he doesn't
run from me."

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:20.069
Shelby Stanga’s arrest

00:04:20.069 --> 00:04:26.120
In October 2014, Shelby "Swamp Man" Stanga
was picked up by the police for cutting down

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:27.729
his neighbor's tree.

00:04:27.729 --> 00:04:32.199
While that might not sound like a big deal,
remember, it does count as destruction of

00:04:32.199 --> 00:04:35.330
private property, vandalism, or both.

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:39.630
Curiously, the cutting took place three years
before the actual arrest.

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:43.669
Apparently, trees have some busy protectors
down there in the bayou.

00:04:43.669 --> 00:04:48.099
"As a matter of fact, kids, I'm swamped."

00:04:48.099 --> 00:04:49.699
Authenticity questions

00:04:49.699 --> 00:04:55.800
Like most reality shows, Ax Men has to deal
with accusations of inauthenticity, many from

00:04:55.800 --> 00:04:58.629
people who work within the logging industry.

00:04:58.629 --> 00:05:03.819
According to some real-life loggers like veteran
Bill Sword, Ax Men presents an overly dramatic

00:05:03.819 --> 00:05:06.370
picture that's pretty far from the truth.

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:08.150
Sword told The Oregonian,

00:05:08.150 --> 00:05:12.059
"Those producers drum up a bunch of baloney
to make it dramatic."

00:05:12.059 --> 00:05:14.210
"Holy s---!"

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:16.370
"Guys, guys!

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:19.610
Get our stuff!

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:22.849
Get our stuff!"

00:05:22.849 --> 00:05:25.009
"Aww f---!"

00:05:25.009 --> 00:05:26.089
"Lookout!

00:05:26.089 --> 00:05:27.169
Ahhh!"

00:05:27.169 --> 00:05:29.330
"Lookout below!"

00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:31.430
Hmmm...you be the judge.

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:32.430
Thanks for watching!

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:36.650
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:05:36.650 --> 00:05:39.909
And leave us a comment to let us know what
you think of Ax Men...

